{"operation": "CGS-RUN", "event": "commit_end", "message": "cgitsync3.9.1 Once published in PyPi A user can now install cgitsync with one command, pipx install complexgitsync, needing only Git and Python 3.11 or newer: the package page has its links, and the source archive no longer carries the developer files. CI now builds the package, installs it the way a user would and runs a real workspace outside the checkout; a tag-driven release workflow is written but has not been run or published. The README and getting-started guide now give users and contributors separate routes, a changelog starts, and bootstrap no longer assumes Pixi.", "committed": 4}
